## Air
component-air = Air
component-air-made-of-part = nitrogen
component-air-made-of-part-2 = oxygen
component-air-made-of-part-3 = argon
component-air-description-novice = The mixture of gases around us: mostly nitrogen and oxygen. It conducts heat poorly — that is why warm clothes and double windows keep heat in.
component-air-description-school = Air conducts heat at ≈ 0.026 W/(m·K) — 20 times less than water. Still air is one of the best heat insulators.
component-air-model-notes = The composition of air is approximate, by mass; in the model air is one substance with its own properties.
